& [Purpose]
  + compile one supplied exact two-part Cantor bootstrap-runtime plus installation-SOP seed into one deterministic provider-free runtime-closure plan and independently verify the complete result
  + account for every expected Cantor-managed runtime file without treating development caches external reservoirs prerequisites or secret custody as additional initiating authority

& [ProfilesAndBounds]
  + [RIS-001] request profile is cantor-runtime-closure-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-runtime-closure-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-runtime-closure-verification/0.1
  + [RIS-002] strict compact UTF-8 canonical JSON denies unknown duplicate and trailing properties and is bounded to 1048576 bytes depth 32 fields 4096 and text 4096
  + [RIS-003] nodes are 2 through 256 edges 0 through 254 edge inputs 1 through 16 prerequisites 0 through 128 evidence references 1 through 64 compatibility references 0 through 32 per node and total declared material bytes 0 through 1099511627776 with checked arithmetic

& [TwoRootSeed]
  + [RIS-004] roots are exactly one BootstrapRuntimeIdentity and one InstallationSOPIdentity with distinct nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing SemanticIds
  + [RIS-005] bootstrap identity binds expected executable lower-case SHA256 expected bytes interface parser verifier planner materializer receipt-capability profiles and one admitted-host-tuple reference without observing an executable or host
  + [RIS-006] SOP identity binds expected canonical-source SHA256 expected bytes satisfaction-signature identity selected-runtime-profile closure-root identity and capability ceiling without embedding external material bytes
  + [RIS-007] the two root material nodes exactly match their seed descriptors and kinds bootstrap_runtime and installation_sop; neither root has a producer

& [MaterialAndPrerequisiteForms]
  + [RIS-008] each MaterialNode binds distinct SemanticId closed kind expected lower-case SHA256 expected bytes provenance reference zero through 32 compatibility references one portable target one verifier profile and executable disposition
  + [RIS-009] nonroot material kinds are derived built acquired explicitly_supplied or generated_configuration and remain semantically distinct
  + [RIS-010] each Prerequisite binds distinct identity closed kind exact nonsecret reference required disposition and unresolved reason; secret private key credential token or protected value bytes are prohibited
  + [RIS-011] every source descriptor is exactly supplied_descriptor deterministic_transform content_addressed_artifact source_build or generated_configuration and binds immutable expected identity; mutable locator latest tag range ambient lookup and unpinned substitution refuse

& [ProducerGraph]
  + [RIS-012] every nonroot node has exactly one ProducerEdge and each edge has one unique nonroot output one through sixteen unique existing inputs one source descriptor one transform profile and expected output SHA256 and bytes exactly matching the output node
  + [RIS-013] every node is reachable from either root, every edge output is unique, no root is produced, and cycles unreachable nodes missing inputs duplicate inputs ambiguous producers and output mismatch refuse
  + [RIS-014] compiler derives lexicographically tie-broken topological order and normalizes nodes prerequisites edges edge inputs compatibility references and evidence references rather than trusting request order

& [LogicalTargets]
  + [RIS-015] target is one through sixteen slash-separated lower-ASCII segments, total one through 240 bytes, each containing only lower-case letters digits dot underscore or hyphen and excluding empty dot and dot-dot segments
  + [RIS-016] backslash colon drive UNC device alternate-stream absolute link symlink reparse and case-fold semantics are inexpressible or refused; exact targets are globally unique
  + [RIS-017] target declarations prove no directory file permission executable bit link layout compatibility or installed state

& [Compilation]
  + [RIS-018] accepted compilation emits compiled_effectless_runtime_closure_plan_only with normalized roots graph order unresolved prerequisite identities capability denials expected receipt template request digest and plan digest
  + [RIS-019] request plan envelope and expected receipt digests are domain-separated deterministic and self-excluding; equal semantic inputs including permutations compile byte identically
  + [RIS-020] expected receipt template binds plan closure node and target identities but has zero observations verifier results materialization actions installation state activation state or successor-recognition authority
  + [RIS-021] evidence references are one through sixty-four unique bounded opaque references and prove only retained evidence addressability

& [AuthorityAndLifecycle]
  + [RIS-022] lifecycle stages declaration compilation resolution materialization installation observation acceptance activation successor recognition rollback and cleanup remain distinct
  + [RIS-023] exact capability denials are filesystem_read filesystem_write filesystem_delete environment_read clock_read process_spawn shell_exec compiler_exec package_manager_exec network_contact artifact_download provider_contact model_load inference mcp_contact git_mutation workspace_mutation secret_access permission_change service_activation cleanup rollback remote_access hardware_effect and external_effect
  + [RIS-024] hashes prove byte correspondence only and never provenance license policy trust compatibility safety semantic suitability availability acquisition installation activation or receipt truth
  + [RIS-025] existing seeded-compiler candidate receipt PreparedRuntime and boot-session forms may be referenced only by exact identity and invariant and are never relabeled as runtime inflation completion

& [VerificationAndFailure]
  + [RIS-026] independent verification reparses exact retained request bytes recompiles the plan and byte-compares request envelope plan verification and manifest identities without trusting producer order digests or claimed counts
  + [RIS-027] verification reports exact node edge root prerequisite unresolved denial evidence target and effect counts and every effect counter is zero
  + [RIS-028] unknown duplicate overbound identifier digest root kind node edge source prerequisite target path graph order authority lifecycle digest receipt verification and fully redigested semantic mutations fail closed with typed faults and no partial output
  + [RIS-029] production exposes supplied-data parsing validation hashing normalization serialization compilation and verification only and performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model MCP Git workspace remote hardware or external action
  + [RIS-030] the first retained acceptance fixture is small synthetic local provider-free secret-free model-free and contains no externally acquired byte

& [Acceptance]
  + [RIS-A01] source audit constraints delineation data dual threat seven-fold canonical explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof review and satisfaction signature agree exactly
  + [RIS-A02] safe Rust exports strict bounded forms deterministic compiler domain-separated digests typed faults expected-receipt forms and independent verifier using existing dependencies only
  + [RIS-A03] focused positive two-permutation byte replay structural path graph bound ambient secret raw-byte and fully redigested semantic-tamper tests plus bounded CLIs retained evidence and separate verifier pass debug and overflow-checked release
  + [RIS-A04] exact locked offline serialized workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format formation runtime evidence recursive evidence attribution publication remote equality and post-push replay pass
  + [RIS-A05] RIS-P1 materialization RIS-P2 artifact and host profiles RIS-P3 activation bootstrap distribution dependency vendoring model/provider acquisition license acceptance secret values remote machines FPGA Minecraft and every physical effect remain separately sourced and signed

& [Invalidation]
  + source root material prerequisite source edge path graph bound digest receipt authority lifecycle denial effect dependency requirement support artifact binding or attribution drift
